WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.366 --> 00:00:10.387
Billy followed one of the elves into Santa's workshop.

2
00:00:11.647 --> 00:00:14.008
The elves were very busy packing up toys.

3
00:00:15.668 --> 00:00:19.269
Billy wanted to help, but the elves were too busy to tell him how.

4
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.750
Billy decided to go look for his father.

5
00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:29.292
He saw his father talking to Santa Claus near the reindeer stables.

6
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.981
Billy didn't want to bother him, so he went into the stables instead.

7
00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:43.243
Billy had never seen reindeer before, and he thought they were very big.

8
00:00:44.584 --> 00:00:51.165
Billy looked at the biggest one and said, "Wow, you're much bigger than I thought you would be."

9
00:00:53.426 --> 00:00:58.347
The reindeer nodded and said, "Yes, many people say that."

10
00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:00.468
"Did you say something?"

11
00:01:01.368 --> 00:01:01.989
asked Billy.

12
00:01:03.269 --> 00:01:04.770
Animals aren't supposed to talk!

13
00:01:06.591 --> 00:01:09.893
"Yes, I did," said the reindeer matter-of-factly.

14
00:01:09.913 --> 00:01:11.514
"My name is Dasher.

15
00:01:11.914 --> 00:01:12.615
What's your name?"

16
00:01:15.116 --> 00:01:15.997
Billy understood.

17
00:01:17.317 --> 00:01:20.299
They were Santa's reindeer, so of course they could talk.

18
00:01:20.319 --> 00:01:22.600
"My name is Billy.

19
00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:25.322
Santa said you were sick.

20
00:01:25.882 --> 00:01:27.163
Are you feeling better?"

21
00:01:27.924 --> 00:01:28.424
he asked.

22
00:01:29.664 --> 00:01:31.906
"We're not sick," said Dasher sadly.

23
00:01:31.926 --> 00:01:33.887
"We're just really sad.

24
00:01:34.307 --> 00:01:36.128
We can't fly if we're sad."

25
00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:42.593
"Oh, just like Peter Pan," said Billy.

26
00:01:43.613 --> 00:01:49.277
"When he taught Wendy and the boys to fly, he said they had to think happy thoughts."

27
00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:52.619
Dasher nodded.

28
00:01:52.639 --> 00:01:59.404
"Yes, that's right, but it's hard to think happy thoughts when everyone is so busy.

29
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.402
Santa doesn't have time for us anymore.

30
00:02:02.903 --> 00:02:04.664
We're lonely and we miss him."

31
00:02:06.606 --> 00:02:13.732
Billy looked at Dasher and said, "If I bring Santa in here right now, will that make you

32
00:02:13.812 --> 00:02:18.196
happy?" "Nothing can bring Santa in here on Christmas Eve.

33
00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:21.378
He's too busy," said Dasher tearfully.

34
00:02:24.621 --> 00:02:31.409
Billy didn't want to see Dasher cry, so he said, "But if I bring Santa in here, would

35
00:02:31.449 --> 00:02:32.649
that make you happy?"

36
00:02:33.449 --> 00:02:42.172
Dasher was sobbing quietly, so he didn't answer, but Comet, Cupid, and Vixen said, "Yes, that would make

37
00:02:42.272 --> 00:02:43.392
us very happy."

38
00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:50.114
Billy left the stable and ran to find his father and Santa Claus.

39
00:02:51.574 --> 00:02:55.075
He found them in Santa's workshop, looking into a microscope.

40
00:02:55.095 --> 00:03:01.745
"Well, it's not an infection," said Doctor Vinton, stepping away from the microscope.

41
00:03:07.388 --> 00:03:10.749
know what's wrong with the reindeer, Daddy," said Billy.

42
00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:13.510
"They're too sad to fly.

43
00:03:14.091 --> 00:03:15.971
It's just like Peter Pan."

44
00:03:16.972 --> 00:03:22.934
Billy's father looked at Billy and said gently, "Billy, Peter Pan is a fairy tale.

45
00:03:23.454 --> 00:03:25.935
This is real, and the problem is real."

46
00:03:28.704 --> 00:03:34.787
Santa stopped looking in the microscope and asked Billy, "Why are they sad?"

47
00:03:34.807 --> 00:03:41.129
"They're sad because you no longer have time to visit with them," said Billy.

48
00:03:41.149 --> 00:03:44.711
"They miss you and they want to see you."

49
00:03:46.791 --> 00:03:52.394
Santa turned to Billy's father and said, "Peter Pan is not a fairy tale.

50
00:03:52.414 --> 00:03:55.035
I knew Peter many years ago.

51
00:03:55.755 --> 00:04:00.570
He was such a wonderful boy, but like all boys, he grew up.

52
00:04:01.431 --> 00:04:04.013
I think Billy has solved our problem.

53
00:04:04.674 --> 00:04:08.457
If my reindeer are unhappy, they can't fly.

54
00:04:09.218 --> 00:04:11.740
Only happy reindeer can fly."

55
00:04:13.521 --> 00:04:16.604
Santa Claus left his workshop and went to the stables.

56
00:04:18.185 --> 00:04:19.467
Billy and his father waited.

57
00:04:20.808 --> 00:04:23.330
After a very long time, Santa returned.

58
00:04:24.351 --> 00:04:25.392
He was very happy.

59
00:04:26.596 --> 00:04:29.177
"Billy, you have saved Christmas.

60
00:04:29.697 --> 00:04:32.579
Thank you for making my reindeer happy.

61
00:04:32.599 --> 00:04:36.300
Ho, ho, ho!"

62
00:04:38.401 --> 00:04:40.742
Billy watched the elves load Santa's sleigh.

63
00:04:42.243 --> 00:04:47.445
Even though the elves kept putting more and more toys into the sleigh, the pile never got bigger.

64
00:04:50.406 --> 00:04:54.188
When the elves finished loading the sleigh, Santa came with his reindeer.

65
00:04:55.564 --> 00:04:59.308
Dasher came up to Billy and said, "Thank you, Billy.

66
00:04:59.648 --> 00:05:02.812
Giving Santa back to us was a wonderful Christmas present.

67
00:05:03.412 --> 00:05:05.574
I hope Santa gives you something special."

68
00:05:05.594 --> 00:05:11.320
"Oh, I'm sure he will," said Billy happily.

69
00:05:12.381 --> 00:05:20.683
As Santa and his reindeer took off, Santa shouted down to Billy, his father, and the elves: "Merry

70
00:05:20.703 --> 00:05:25.154
Christmas to all, and to all a good night!

71
00:05:25.475 --> 00:05:26.497
Ho, ho, ho!"
